(Now we need to ensure we have not origin_node_occupied and not destination_node_occupied (they start false, we never load payloads, so they remain false). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not origin_availability_locked etc before locking.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not origin_availability_confirmed before locking? Actually lock_origin_availability effect sets origin_availability_confirmed true. Precondition requires not origin_availability_locked. It does not require not origin_availability_confirmed. So we can lock even if not confirmed yet; after lock we get confirmed. Good.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not destination_availability_locked etc.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not transport_leg_loading_authorized before authorizing.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not transport_leg_assembled before assembling.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not origin_leg_loaded and not destination_leg_loaded (they start false, and we never set them true because we use assemble_transport_leg which does not set them). So they remain false.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not loading_container_loaded before loading.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_staged_for_loading before staging.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_loading_verified before verifying.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_clearance_established before establishing.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_finalized before finalize.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not dispatched before execute.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not dispatch_allocated before allocate_dispatch_slot.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_task_profile_linked before attach_task_profile (precondition requires not? Actually attach_task_profile precondition: candidate_created ?candidate, vehicle_allocated ?candidate, route_task_profile_available ?route_task_profile. It does not require not candidate_task_profile_linked. So we could attach multiple times? But effect adds candidate_task_profile_linked and removes route_task_profile_available. If we attach again when already linked, we would need route_task_profile_available which would be false, so precondition fails. So we need to detach before reattaching.)
(Thus we need to detach after we are done with each candidate's use of task profile.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_vehicle_linked before allocate_vehicle_unit (precondition requires not vehicle_allocated). So we need to ensure we haven't already allocated vehicle to that candidate.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_dispatch_slot_linked before allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate (precondition requires not dispatch_allocated). Effect adds candidate_dispatch_slot_linked and removes dispatch_slot_available.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not dispatch_allocated before execute_schedule_dispatch (precondition requires dispatch_allocated). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not dispatched before execute.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not destination_availability_locked before lock_destination_availability.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not destination_availability_confirmed before lock? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not origin_availability_locked before lock_origin_availability.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_operator_linked before assign_operator_resource (precondition requires candidate_prepared and operator_available; does not require not candidate_operator_linked). Effect adds candidate_operator_linked and removes operator_available. So if already linked, we cannot assign again because operator_available false. So we need to release before reassigning.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_skill_certificate_linked before assign_skill_certificate (precondition requires candidate_prepared and skill_certificate_available). Effect adds link and removes skill_certificate_available.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_compliance_certificate_linked before assign_compliance_certificate (precondition requires candidate_prepared and compliance_certificate_available). Effect adds link and removes compliance_certificate_available.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not loading_container_leg_linked before load_container_onto_leg? Actually load_container_onto_leg effect adds loading_container_leg_linked; precondition does not require not loading_container_leg_linked. So we could link multiple containers to same leg; but we need to ensure loading_container_available is true for each container we load.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not loading_container_loaded before load_container_onto_leg.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_staged_for_loading before stage_schedule_candidate.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_loading_verified before verify_loading_profile_nominal.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not candidate_clearance_established before establish_clearance_nominal.)
(Now we need to ensure we have not route_sequence_context_set before finalize_candidate_direct? Actually finalize_candidate_direct precondition includes not route_sequence_context_set ?candidate. So we need to ensure that is false. We never set route_sequence_context_set for shiftA unless we use establish_clearance_nominal which sets route_sequence_context_set as effect. Indeed establish_clearance_nominal effect includes (route_sequence_context_set ?candidate). So after establishing clearance, route_sequence_context_set becomes true. Then finalize_candidate_direct precondition requires not route_sequence_context_set ?candidate, which would fail. So we cannot use finalize_candidate_direct after establish_clearance_nominal because it sets route_sequence_context_set. Wait check: establish_clearance_nominal effect: (candidate_clearance_established ?candidate) (route_sequence_context_set ?candidate). Yes. finalize_candidate_direct precondition: (candidate_clearance_established ?candidate) (not (route_sequence_context_set ?candidate)) (not (candidate_finalized ?candidate)). So after establishing clearance_nominal, route_sequence_context_set becomes true, violating the not route_sequence_context_set precondition. So we cannot use finalize_candidate_direct after establish_clearance_nominal. We need to use either finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation or finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation. Let's check those.)
(finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation precondition: (candidate_clearance_established ?candidate) (route_sequence_validated ?candidate) (not (candidate_finalized ?candidate)). Effect: (candidate_finalized ?candidate) (dispatch_ready ?candidate). So we need route_sequence_validated.)
(finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation precondition: (compliance_validation_complete ?candidate) (not (candidate_finalized ?candidate)). Effect: (candidate_finalized ?candidate) (dispatch_ready ?candidate). So we need compliance_validation_complete.)
(Thus we have two options after establishing clearance: either validate route sequence (needs service window etc) or complete compliance validation (needs operator alignment confirmed and compliance certificate linked). Since we already have compliance certificate linked (we will have it for establish_clearance_nominal), we could go the compliance validation path: after establishing clearance, we need to confirm operator alignment (confirm_operator_alignment) which requires constraint_applied and candidate_operator_linked. Then verify_compliance_certificate (requires operator_alignment_confirmed and candidate_compliance_certificate_linked). Then finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation.)
(Alternatively we could go route sequence validation path: after establishing clearance, we need to set route sequence context (already set by establish_clearance_nominal), attach service window, validate route sequence (requires service_window linked, origin/destination availability confirmed, etc). That may be simpler? Let's examine.)
(We already have route_sequence_context_set true after establish_clearance_nominal. To validate route sequence we need: candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_context_set, candidate_service_window_linked, candidate_origin_availability_linked, candidate_destination_availability_linked, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, candidate_task_profile_linked, not route_sequence_validated.)
(Thus we need to attach service window to shiftA, and have origin/destination availabilities confirmed (they will be after locking). We also need candidate_task_profile_linked (we have). So we can do route sequence validation path.)
(Thus after establishing clearance_nominal, we can:)
(- attach_service_window shiftA service_window_alpha (or beta))
(- validate_route_sequence shiftA oriA destA taskP service_window_alpha)
(- finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation shiftA (gives dispatch_ready and candidate_finalized))
(Thus we avoid needing compliance validation path (which would require operator alignment confirmed etc). This path uses service window.)
(Thus we need to attach a service window to shiftA. We have two service windows available initially. We'll need to attach one, then after validation we could detach? Not needed; we can keep it linked; not needed for goal.)
(Thus we need to allocate a service window (make it not available). That's fine.)
(Thus shiftA path:)
(- create_candidate shiftA)
(- allocate vehicle (vehA))
(- attach_task_profile shiftA taskP)
(- confirm_candidate_preparedness shiftA taskP)
(- load_container_onto_leg shiftA contA leg (need transport leg assembled and loading authorized))
(- stage_schedule_candidate shiftA contB? Wait loading container for shiftA is contA. Stage requires loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked (we will have after load). Good.)
(- verify_loading_profile_nominal shiftA skill op contA leg (need skill cert and operator linked))
(- establish_clearance_nominal shiftA comp contA leg)
(- attach_service_window shiftA service_window_alpha (or beta))
(- validate_route_sequence shiftA oriA destA taskP service_window_alpha)
(- finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation shiftA)
(- allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate shiftA dispSlot taskP)
(- execute_schedule_dispatch shiftA vehA dispSlot)
(Now after execute_schedule_dispatch, vehicle_unit_alpha becomes available again, dispatch_slot becomes available.)
(Now we need to handle oriA and destA dispatch.)
(We need to prepare oriA and destA (create, allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm preparedness). We'll need to allocate vehicles: we have vehB and vehC available initially (since we used vehA for shiftA, but after shiftA dispatch vehA becomes available again). However we need to allocate vehicles for oriA and destA before we dispatch them. We can allocate vehB to oriA, vehC to destA. After we dispatch oriA and destA, their vehicles become available again (but we may not need them later). shiftB will need a vehicle later; we can use vehA after shiftA dispatch.)
(Now we need to lock oriA and destA, activate nodes, assemble leg, authorize loading, mark dispatch ready, allocate dispatch slot, execute dispatch.)
(We'll need to attach task profile to oriA and destA before confirm_candidate_preparedness.)
(We'll need to detach task profile after we are done with allocate_dispatch_slot and execute dispatch (since after dispatch we may not need task profile linked; we can detach to free for shiftB later). However we need task profile for oriA and destA for allocate_dispatch_slot and execute dispatch (precondition requires candidate_task_profile_linked). After execute dispatch, we could detach to free task profile for shiftB.)
(Thus we can attach task profile to oriA, confirm preparedness, lock, activate node, etc. After we allocate dispatch slot and execute dispatch, we can detach task profile from oriA (making it available). Similarly for destA)
